ha oysters  a little spicy little smell like a  little bit of kick now  does the green curry one have kik it has  a little kick yeah it has a lots of  serrano peppers  lemongrass  curry paste i might be i hate to say  this i might be more on the match yeah  yeah there's a smoked trout salad with  house made kimchi style ferment and  purple daikon this is like artwork i  don't want to touch it and even an  appetizer inspired by her dad's old  go-to starter called poppy's caviar he  made a version that was sour cream a  really improvised scallion vinaigrette  and then typically like really cheap  salty fish row from the grocery store  aisle that comes in those little jars  right and so we wanted like to mimic  that because it's so enjoyable kind of  hits all the notes on the palette  henrietta red's version includes  homemade saltines and paddle fish caviar  that comes from just outside nashville  what does dad think of this one i think  he's just very kind of tickled to be on  the menu but sullivan traces her  culinary inspiration to another family  on another continent thanks to a high  school study abroad program in france  and i lived with a family that had three  teenage kids who really couldn't care  less that i was there  and so i spent a lot of time with the  mother and the mother had a beautiful  backyard garden and would pull food from  it for us to cook for lunch and dinner  most days and so really that was kind of  the first interest i had in growing food  and cooking food and then kind of grew  and evolved from there especially when  sullivan chose tulane university in new  orleans for college  yeah i don't know if there's a better  food city than new orleans in some ways  yes i think actually i blame my career  path on going to college there  there are a lot of different things  people blame new orleans for that's a  good thing  everything there is about cultural  heritage the restaurants are 100 years  old they all have stories and family  history and i just fell in love with it  and so i started hostessing and then  eventually cooking as a college student  before going on to culinary school  that led to an internship for julio four  egg with dan barber and blue hill at  stone barns followed by a job under  thomas keller at manhattan's per se  but it was at franny's an italian  restaurant in brooklyn where sullivan  says she really cooked for the first  time  they just had a style of cooking that  was so  infused with  warmth and soul and flavor and each dish  only had  really four or five ingredients and so  it was kind of about like sussing out  the best qualities of all those  ingredients and and just letting them  shine and i think it just really opened  my eyes to so much that was outside of  sort of the classical technique  at henrietta red sullivan brought it all  together a variety of technique and  tastes  the sausage is another thing we've  always kept on the menu for the meat  eaters there's a sausage served this  season with orange yogurt and pharaoh  salad oh that's so good yeah that's a  really nice one very orange kind of  fresh oh yeah  vegetarian options include this gnocchi  adorned by melted squash with pepita  seeds and a parmesan broth things just  taste better when they're in season so  if you're using really good ingredients  you don't have to do that much to  manipulate it all helping sullivan and  henrietta redd stand out in a city no  longer known  simply for its music  the fact that we've kind of become a  standby in this scene is pretty amazing  and through a pandemic yes  yeah through a crazy time and i think  that yeah i think that people have come  to sort of know and understand our style  and what we do here and and that is  special what do you hope somebody leaves  here with you know i hope feeling like  they  just had a good time when you're in here  and the dining room's full and there's  music on and it's the right vibe it kind  of feels like a party those are the best  nights for us where it's busy and loud  and they kind of  felt taken care of  and we helped take care of you yay  poppy's caviar which is truly delicious  again that house-made saltine the  homemade  saltine and the paddle fish paddlefish  from the nashville nashville area what  does that mean what do you mean from the  nashville area that's where they get the  tablet that's where they get the caviar  yeah no i know but from a river i  thought it was from an ocean not this  this caviar is from near nashville but  all the oysters that she brings in it's  literally you know gulf coast it's the  east coast the west coast and all of  that  thanks to the beauty of fedex and  technology oh my gosh it's delicious  right oh man so good yes so so good

